---
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="ALife Expo"
	description="A digital public exhibition making artificial life accessible to everyone."
	pubDate={new Date('January 1 2025')}
	heroImage={url('/alife2025.jpg')}
	hideDate={true}
>
	<p>
		The <strong>ALife Expo</strong> is a public-facing, digital exhibition designed to open up the world of artificial life to everyone, with no background required. Growing out of the public expo that Martha Emerson and I curated and organised at ALIFE 2025, it guides visitors through the field's big ideas, such as emergence, self-organisation, evolution, and complexity from simplicity, in a set of accessible, self-contained "zones". It's part of an ongoing effort to make artificial life more engaging, playful, visible, and welcoming to curious minds outside the research community.
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="https://alife-expo.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit the ALife Expo &rarr;</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
